            "body": "Hello @Metsker, \n\nThanks for the issue!\n~~What exact Neovim version do you use? Since v0.12.0, multiple issues where fixed upstream regarding `restart`.~~\n\n~~I cannot reproduce from v0.12.1 and onwards. Using v0.12.0 does not result in an empty buffer, but a message: 'W325: Ignoring swapfile from Nvim process 13535'.~~\n\nEdit:\n~~This notification indeed does not occur using '--clean'.~~\n\n~~I don't think this is a bug in MiniMax, because Neovim v0.12.1 seems to work as expected.~~\n\nEdit:\nApologies, I can reproduce. I expected `cd ~/.config/nvim` as the first step. It does occur when one changes directory into the plugin folder.\n\n",
