        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I indeed can reproduce. *But* interestingly enough, only if calling with `nvim 10_options.lua` and not like `nvim -- 10_options.lua` (in which case it shows a 'mini.starter' buffer).\n\nThe reason here seems to indeed be an [enabled auto root](https://github.com/nvim-mini/MiniMax/blob/c84e697595116e6c2a1a2cf13afe47b832283d48/configs/nvim-0.12/plugin/30_mini.lua#L253). But I'd say this is indeed an upstream Neovim issue, because `:restart` seems to use Neovim's current directory when restarting and not shell's.\n\nThis is reproducible with `nvim --clean 10_options` after `:cd ..` and `:restart`.\n\nThe `MiniMisc.setup_auto_root()` won't go anywhere, so this will either be an expected limitation or will be fixed upstream.",
